The page totals what was invoiced, received and outstanding, per partner and per claim, and **CSV for the bookkeeper** exports every invoice. On a partner''s page, **Invoice settings** holds their usual kickback and billing email. The partner sees their invoices, with how to pay, on their partner page.

## Kickbacks and repair costs in the profit numbers

Every partner invoice counts on a car: the car of its booking or its claim fills in by itself; otherwise choose it with **Car (empty: from the booking or the claim)** in the builder, or **Choose the car** on an invoice already sent. The money received on an invoice is its kickback, before HST, on the day it came in: **Body shop kickback**, **Tow kickback** or **Storage kickback**.

Repair costs are added on the car (**Vehicles**, the car, **Kickbacks and repairs**) or on the claim (the incident''s page): **Add a repair cost**, then the date, the shop or another vendor, what was done, the amount and tax, who paid (CarmaCars, the owner or the insurer), the claim and a receipt. **Change** and **Remove** are on each row.

The totals for a period, by owner and by car, with the CSV: **Company** > **Kickbacks and repairs** for the business, **Kickbacks and repairs** on an owner''s page for their cars, and on a car''s page for the car. Owners see none of this until you press **Show repair costs and kickbacks to this owner** on their **Kickbacks and repairs** tab; then they see their own cars'' lines under Money in their portal.
',
  '<p class="gd-p">Body shops and tow truck companies (and, if you want, dealerships and insurance brokers) can send you renters and earn a kickback when the rental is finished and paid in full. A separate switch adds an optional affiliate link to RentalCoverage on the pages that talk about coverage. Nothing in either program is shown to renters until you set it up.</p><section class="gd-task" id="referral-partners-and-rentalcoverage-add-a-partner" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Add a partner</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">People</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Partners</b>, the <b class="gd-ui">Referral partners</b> tab, then <b class="gd-ui">Add a partner</b>.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Choose the kind (body shop, tow truck company, dealership or insurance broker) and type the business name, the contact, phone and email. Start typing the address: the city and postal code fill in.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Choose how you pay them (e-Transfer, cheque, bank transfer, cash or another way) and, for e-Transfer, the email to pay.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Choose the kickback: a flat amount for each completed rental ($50 unless you change it) or a percentage of the rental charge (10% unless you change it). The percentage applies to the rental charge after discounts only, never to add-ons, fees or taxes. The two defaults are under <b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Program</b>, Referral partners.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Save</b>. A partner you add is active at once, with a code, a short link and a flyer.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="referral-partners-and-rentalcoverage-approve-a-sign-up" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Approve a sign-up</h2><p class="gd-p">The public pages carmacars.ca/partners/body-shops and carmacars.ca/partners/tow-trucks have a sign-up form. A sign-up is a pending partner and a task for you; it earns nothing and its code ties no rental until you approve it.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Open <b class="gd-ui">People</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Partners</b>, the <b class="gd-ui">Referral partners</b> tab. A sign-up shows as Waiting for approval, and the Partners tab shows how many are waiting.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Open the partner and check the business. Press <b class="gd-ui">Approve</b> (or <b class="gd-ui">Decline</b>: they are not told by email).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Write them their link</b>. It opens an email to them with their link and code; attach the flyer from the next section before you send it.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="referral-partners-and-rentalcoverage-the-link-the-qr-code-and-the-flyer" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The link, the QR code and the flyer</h2><p class="gd-p">Open the partner. The card &quot;Link, QR code and flyer&quot; shows everything they hand out.</p><ul class="gd-ul"><li>The short link is carmacars.ca/r/ and their code, for example carmacars.ca/r/BODY1234. A renter who opens it keeps the partner for 60 days on that device, even if they book later.</li><li>Press <b class="gd-ui">Flyer for the counter (PDF)</b> for a one-page flyer with their name, their code and a QR code of the link. Print it or send it.</li><li>A renter can also type the code in &quot;Did someone refer you?&quot; on the request to book. A code typed there wins over the link. A code nobody holds is ignored.</li><li>Changing the code ends the old link, QR code and flyer. Pausing or ending a partner stops new rentals from being tied to them; what they already earned stays.</li></ul></section><section class="gd-task" id="referral-partners-and-rentalcoverage-rentals-you-add-by-hand" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Rentals you add by hand</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Add a rental</b> (on Bookings), field &quot;Referred by (partner code)&quot;.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Type the partner&#39;s code if a body shop or tow truck sent the renter. A code that does not exist or is not active is refused, so a typing mistake shows at once.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Forgot it? Open the partner and press <b class="gd-ui">Tie a booking</b>: enter the booking number and why. This is not possible once a kickback on that booking is approved or paid, nor on a booking that already has an owner or field staff member as its referrer (one referrer per booking: owner, then field staff, then the partner).</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="referral-partners-and-rentalcoverage-earnings-and-payments" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Earnings and payments</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">People</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Partners</b>, the <b class="gd-ui">Referral partners</b> tab, the tabs Partners, Kickbacks and Payments made.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">A kickback starts as &quot;Rental not finished yet&quot;. It is earned when the booking is completed and paid in full and no payment is in dispute; it then waits as &quot;Pending approval&quot;.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Check it on the Kickbacks tab and press <b class="gd-ui">Approve</b> (or <b class="gd-ui">Approve all</b> for one partner).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Pay the partner the way you agreed, then press <b class="gd-ui">Record a payment</b> on their line: it settles every approved kickback and keeps the reference.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">A refund or a lost dispute after the kickback was earned takes it back (a reversal line). If it was already paid, the reversal stays on the ledger as a negative line for you to settle with the partner. Use <b class="gd-ui">Reverse</b> to take one back yourself, with a reason.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>The kickback is a booking expense, taken before the owner&#39;s share is worked out, in the same line as staff commissions on the owner statement. Check the owner agreement wording on kickbacks before you start paying partners.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="referral-partners-and-rentalcoverage-the-partner-s-own-page" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The partner&#39;s own page</h2><p class="gd-p">The card &quot;Link, QR code and flyer&quot; shows a private page address for the partner. Send it only to them.</p><ul class="gd-ul"><li>It shows their link and code, their referrals by the customer&#39;s first name and the month only, what is waiting and what was paid. No sign-in: the long address is the key.</li><li>Press <b class="gd-ui">New private page link</b> if it was shared by mistake: the old address stops working at once.</li></ul></section><section class="gd-task" id="referral-partners-and-rentalcoverage-rentalcoverage-affiliate" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">RentalCoverage affiliate</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">RentalCoverage affiliate</b>. It is off until you join the affiliate program and paste your link.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Join RentalCoverage&#39;s affiliate program (their affiliate dashboard gives you a tracking link, and sometimes an ID).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Paste the affiliate link</b>. Paste the link exactly as the dashboard gives it. If it has {id} in it, type your ID in the next field and it is filled in. Leave &quot;Show the link on the site&quot; ticked and press <b class="gd-ui">Save</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">The link now shows on Requirements and coverage, the credit card coverage guide and the coverage step of the request to book. Each says it is a separate company&#39;s optional product, that it does not replace the coverage option the renter chooses, that CarmaCars may earn a commission and that it costs the renter nothing extra. It says nothing about what the product covers.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Untick &quot;Show the link on the site&quot; any time to turn it off everywhere.</div></li></ol></div><ul class="gd-ul"><li>Every click goes through a CarmaCars address that counts it by place and month (and by booking when the renter has one) and adds utm_source=carmacars, utm_medium=referral and utm_campaign=coverage_ and the place.</li><li>The page shows clicks by place and month and the latest clicks. RentalCoverage reports the sales, not the site: when they pay you, press <b class="gd-ui">Add a payment received</b> with the date, amount and reference.</li></ul></section><section class="gd-task" id="referral-partners-and-rentalcoverage-invoices-to-partners-release-28" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Invoices to partners (release 28)</h2><p class="gd-p">Body shops, tow trucks and storage yards owe us their kickback on claim, towing or storage money. <b class="gd-ui">Referral partners</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Invoices</b>:</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">New invoice to a partner</b>: the partner, what it is for, the claim number, insurer, vehicle and customer, and the partner&#39;s own total.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">The lines: the wording (Outsourced repair, towing or storage services, editable), a percentage of the partner&#39;s total (the partner&#39;s usual kickback fills it) or a quantity and amount, and HST 13% on or off per line.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Save and send to the partner</b>: the invoice gets its number (PI-000001 and on), a due date, and is emailed to the partner&#39;s billing email with a link to the PDF. <b class="gd-ui">Send again</b> any time. One reminder goes before and one after the due date (the days are on the invoice; 0 for none).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Record money received</b>: cheque, e-Transfer or cash, the amount, the date, the reference and a photo of the cheque if you have one (View opens it later). The invoice shows partly paid, paid or overdue.</div></li></ol></div><p class="gd-p">The page totals what was invoiced, received and outstanding, per partner and per claim, and <b class="gd-ui">CSV for the bookkeeper</b> exports every invoice. On a partner&#39;s page, <b class="gd-ui">Invoice settings</b> holds their usual kickback and billing email. The partner sees their invoices, with how to pay, on their partner page.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="referral-partners-and-rentalcoverage-kickbacks-and-repair-costs-in-the-profit-numbers" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Kickbacks and repair costs in the profit numbers</h2><p class="gd-p">Every partner invoice counts on a car: the car of its booking or its claim fills in by itself; otherwise choose it with <b class="gd-ui">Car (empty: from the booking or the claim)</b> in the builder, or <b class="gd-ui">Choose the car</b> on an invoice already sent. The money received on an invoice is its kickback, before HST, on the day it came in: <b class="gd-ui">Body shop kickback</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Tow kickback</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Storage kickback</b>.</p><p class="gd-p">Repair costs are added on the car (<b class="gd-ui">Vehicles</b>, the car, <b class="gd-ui">Kickbacks and repairs</b>) or on the claim (the incident&#39;s page): <b class="gd-ui">Add a repair cost</b>, then the date, the shop or another vendor, what was done, the amount and tax, who paid (CarmaCars, the owner or the insurer), the claim and a receipt. <b class="gd-ui">Change</b> and <b class="gd-ui">Remove</b> are on each row.</p><p class="gd-p">The totals for a period, by owner and by car, with the CSV: <b class="gd-ui">Company</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Kickbacks and repairs</b> for the business, <b class="gd-ui">Kickbacks and repairs</b> on an owner&#39;s page for their cars, and on a car&#39;s page for the car. Owners see none of this until you press <b class="gd-ui">Show repair costs and kickbacks to this owner</b> on their <b class="gd-ui">Kickbacks and repairs</b> tab; then they see their own cars&#39; lines under Money in their portal.</p></section>');
select app.guide_release_section('admin', 'hiring', 'chapter', 'referral-partners-and-rentalcoverage', 'Candidates apply on carmacars.ca/careers. Every application is scored on the server against the role''s rubric: a candidate who passes gets a link to book a 15-minute call, one who does not qualify for Field staff is offered Sales instead, and the rest wait for you. During each call you fill in a rubric; the final score ranks everyone in the role.

## Open a role and send the apply link

**People** > **Hiring**, tab Roles and links.

1. Press **Open the role** to put it on carmacars.ca/careers (and in the sitemap and the footer); **Close the role** takes it off. Field staff, Sales in person and Remote sales start open; the three remote assistant roles start closed.
2. Copy the apply link: it ends with ?src=indeed (or ?src=onlinejobs for the remote roles), so each application records where it came from.
3. Copy the message under it and paste it into Indeed (or OnlineJobs.ph) messages to each applicant. It asks them to answer the role''s questions, about five minutes.
4. **Pass mark and pay** changes the pass mark (60 of 100 unless you change it) and the pay shown on the page.

## What happens to each application

The database scores the answers the moment they arrive. The candidate never sees the points.

- Score at or above the pass mark, no knock-out: an email with a personal link to book a call (Invited). A remote assistant (customer service, fleet, finance, remote sales) gets a link to a recorded AI interview instead, while AI interviews are on (see below).
- Field staff who do not qualify (no full G licence, under three years of driving, or a low score) are not declined: they get a friendly email offering Sales in person, with a one-click link that fills in their details, and Remote sales named as the other choice (Referred). If they already applied for Sales, nothing is sent and a note says so.
- Sales in person below the pass mark, or remote only, is offered Remote sales. A remote assistant role below the pass mark is offered the closest other open role.
- A knock-out with no other role to offer (for example the finance code word missing) gets a polite decline.
- Anyone else waits for you as Below the bar, with only a confirmation email.

## Review the applications

**People** > **Hiring**, tab Applications.

1. Filter by role, status, source (Indeed, OnlineJobs.ph, website, referral) or score. Open a candidate for every answer with the points it earned and any knock-out.
2. **Invite anyway** sends the booking link to a candidate below the bar, declined or referred. **Decline** sends the polite decline email (untick it to decline without an email).
3. A candidate referred to another role shows the link both ways under Linked applications.

## Interview days

**People** > **Hiring**, tab Interview days.

1. Press **Add an interview day**: the day, from and to (Toronto time), the call length (15 minutes) and the break between calls (5 minutes), phone or video, and the roles it is for (empty: every role).
2. Phone: you call the candidate on the number they gave. Video: every booking gets its own Jitsi Meet link, in the candidate''s email and on their page.
3. Candidates book, move or cancel from their link. They get a confirmation, a reminder the evening before and one an hour before (and a text, when phone and texts are on). Remote roles show Manila time too.
4. **Turn off** stops new bookings on a day; a day with bookings cannot be deleted.

## Run the calls with the rubric

**People** > **Hiring**, tab Calls.

1. Pick the day. Each call shows the time, the candidate, Call (or the video link). Press **Start**.
2. The rubric sits beside the call guide (what to ask each minute, and what a good answer sounds like). Score each line 1 to 5: Communication, Reliability and availability, Role skills, Customer or sales instinct, Judgement on the scenarios, Attitude.
3. Choose the decision (Hire, Maybe, No, No show), add notes and press **Save the rubric**. The interview score (of 100) and the final score (40% screening, 60% interview) fill in, with the rank in the role.

## Shortlist and Hire

**People** > **Hiring**, tab Shortlist.

1. Each role lists its interviewed candidates by final score, rank 1 first.
2. Open the candidate and press **Hire**. It invites them into the right portal: field staff, or the assistant portal (both sales roles are the Sales function, with in person or remote recorded).
3. Then press **Send the agreement to sign**: check the values and send the staff agreement to sign in their portal.
4. **Not hired** closes a candidate after the call without an email; **Withdrawn** is for one who no longer wants the role.

> Good to know: Applications are for Admins only. The name, contact details and answers of a candidate who is not hired are deleted 12 months after the decision, as the privacy policy says.


> Good to know: A candidate who passes while no interview day is open for their role is invited but waits: the invitation email goes when you add (or open) a day for that role. The Hiring page shows "N applicants invited but no interview day is open for" the role, with **Add an interview day**. Candidates who already had the email, or opened their link and found no time ("No call times are open right now"), get "New times are open" when the day is added.

## Decisions and the emails they send

The rubric''s **Decision** is Hire, Maybe, No, **Good fit for Sales instead** or No show. Recording one sends nothing.

1. **Good fit for Sales instead** refers the candidate to Sales: Sales in person for Field staff and Sales in person, Remote Sales for the remote roles. If they already applied for that Sales role, their Sales application gets a note for the shortlist and no email goes.
2. Open **Hiring**, **Emails to send**: every decided candidate with the email that will go (Hire: the next steps; Sales: the offer with the one-click apply link; No: the polite decline; No show: the polite no-show email). Maybe sends nothing.
3. **Change** a row (the decision, the email on or off, a personal line for the hire and no-show emails) or **Undo** it (the rubric goes back to Maybe).
4. Press **Send all decision emails**. Choose **Now**, next Monday at 9:00 am Toronto, tomorrow at 9:00 am, or another time. Each candidate gets one email, never twice; the statuses follow (referred, Not hired, No show). Hire still needs **Hire** with the staff account.

## AI interviews for the remote roles

Remote assistants who pass screening take a short recorded interview on their own, from their phone or computer, instead of a live call. In-person roles keep their phone calls. **People** > **Hiring**, tab Roles and links, card AI interviews for the remote roles: **Turn off** sends the remote roles the booking link again.

1. The candidate gets one email, **Start my interview**. The link works 7 days; no reminders, no texts.
2. They agree to the recording first. Then nine questions from the role''s rubric: experience, the role''s skills, social media, what CarmaCars does and the shift, the role''s scenario, the hours and the pay, internet and backup, education and other jobs, career and moving to Canada. Each is shown and read aloud; they answer out loud (or type). Where an answer is vague the AI asks a short follow-up, two at most.
3. When the last answer is in, the candidate is **Interviewed**. Within minutes the AI scores each rubric line 1 to 5 with a quote from the answers, judges the spoken English, lists anything to check, and recommends: **Invite to a live call**, **Hire**, **Decline** or **Good fit for Sales instead**. Hiring shows "N AI interviews done and waiting for your decision".
4. Open the candidate. The AI interview card has the recommendation and the scores, then every answer in order: play the recording, read the transcript.
5. You decide, as after a call: the rubric''s **Decision**, then **Emails to send**. Or press **Invite to a live call**: the candidate gets the link to book a video call (they wait for an interview day like everyone else).
6. A link that expired: **New interview link** emails a new one for 7 days; the answers given are kept.

> Good to know: The AI never hires or declines anyone: nothing goes to the candidate until you send the decision emails. Transcripts and scores use the free Workers AI allowance (Settings > Usage, "Hiring interviews"); when today''s share is used, the answer is kept and the transcript or the scores come later by themselves. The recordings and transcripts are deleted with the application, 12 months after the decision.

## Phone or video, and the remote calls confirmed

- The way a call is held follows the role: Field staff and Sales in person are called by phone (record it with Quo), the remote roles meet by video (a Jitsi link in their emails). An interview day''s **How** is only the default shown.
- Remote candidates get no reminders and no texts. 24 hours before the call (at once if they book closer than that) they get one email with **Confirm my call** (one press, no sign-in). Not confirmed within 12 hours of that email, or by 1 hour before the call, the call is cancelled, the time opens again and they get a short email with the link to book again.
- **Calls** shows **Confirmed**, **Waiting** or **Asked 24 hours before** for each remote call, and **Cancelled: not confirmed** for the last 7 days. The in-person roles keep their reminders.
', 'Hiring', 'Open roles and apply links for Indeed and OnlineJobs.ph, the applications and their scores, AI interviews for the remote roles, interview days, the rubric during each call, the ranked shortlist and Hire.',
